Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): add a project memory that refuses secrets and
 mistrusts summaries

Fourth slice: the engineering memory from the task, minus its persistence.

core/memory:
- MemoryFact carries its source (SOURCE_CODE / BUILD_OUTPUT / USER / REPO_DOC /
  AGENT_SUMMARY), the commit it was true of, and when it was verified. Both
  facts are needed: the commit says what it was true of, the clock says how
  long ago.
- A fact from AGENT_SUMMARY is always returned with needsVerification = true
  until markVerified() is called against the current head - a model's summary
  is a pointer to look somewhere, not an answer.
- A fact whose commit no longer matches the head, or whose verification is
  older than the age limit, is returned as unverified with the reason ("recorded
  at 414c780, head is 1a8a67a", "verified 15 days ago").
- Every fact is screened with the same SecretRedaction patterns the crash
  reporter uses plus a private-key header check, and refused outright rather
  than stored scrubbed; the rejection never names the matched pattern.
- record() refuses different text under an existing id, so a decision is not
  silently overwritten.
- recall() ranks by keyword overlap and stops at a character budget, reporting
  how many facts it omitted; CONSTRAINT facts are always included because the
  rules that must not be broken are worth the space.
- Bounded (400 facts) and thread safe.

docs/PROJECT_MEMORY.md also states the split the task asks for: reviewable
architectural knowledge lives in tracked markdown, operational facts here.

